 α, Gallai), so the minimum cover avoiding the least vertex of a symmetric","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"difference. Every vertex with a self-loop is in it; parallel edges count once. The cost is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"maximumIndependentSet()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s: O(m √n) on bipartite components.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumVertexCover()","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumvertexcover()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumVertexCover","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"minimumVertexCover()"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/independenceNumber()":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"independenceNumber"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"}],"url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/independencenumber()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The size of a maximum independent set, α: 0 for the empty graph. A bipartite component"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"contributes its vertex count minus a maximum matching (König), a complete one 1, any other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the reductions and kernel search of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maximumIndependentSet()"},{"type":"text","text":" once, without its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lexicographic pass: O(n + m) plus the search on what the reductions leave."}],"title":"independenceNumber()","identifier":"doc: